Well, there are player who play for years without ascending. With a
little note-taking they can easily build their own shopping spoiler.

But probably people who can't ascend after years don't take notes. I
myself didn't ascend a character until I started to take notes. This
immediately improved my survival probability. I started to think
harder about the death of a character and how I could have prevented
it.

> Very easy to circumvent this problem. Just drop the items to get the
> price, and it's a possible "collision of prices", just leave the shop,
> go back in, and try again. The chance of prices being one third off is
> less than 50%, so if you try the ducious scrolls a few times this way,
> you are almost sure what they really are. It just takes a few turns
> more.

I'm not sure if I understand you correctly. The one third off appears
only when you try to buy things in a shop. But then also the charisma
is involved and as this value can change a lot in a game, I usually
don't bother.

When I price-ID an item, I usually own the item and offer it a few
times to the shopkeeper. For example a fizzy potion at the convenient
slot d:
What do you want to drop? [$a-su-x or ?*] 
 Pressing d
You drop a fizzy potion.--More--
 Pressing SPACE
Gorlowka offers 100 gold pieces for your fizzy potion.  Sell it? [ynaq] (y) 
 Pressing n
 Pressing ,
d - a fizzy potion.
-> repeat until a different value is shown. In this case 75gp is the
value with one quarter off.

It usually doesn't take more then 5 seconds for the two values to
appear.

